Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Meridian Nine Swallows Its Signal
- Story & Context: Recorded during a total blackout at the abandoned Cape Hope lighthouse, this opening piece captured the exact moment a rogue weather balloon collapsed into the surf while two cargo barges blew their horns in an accidental C-sharp triad. Maren Vance tracked the low whistle takes using an old ribbon microphone suspended down a fifty-foot ventilation shaft to catch the ocean draft. The session was nearly abandoned when the wind cut the power, leaving only the sound of creaking timber and breathing flutes on the master tape. Vance later overdubbed a single line of whispered vocal, singing, "We marked the shelf where the saltwater turned to glass."
