- Story & Context: The EP closes with a sprawling mythic track detailing a local urban legend about a ghost ship that guides lost orbital debris back into the ocean bed using low-frequency acoustic vibrations. Recorded live in a single take inside an empty dry dock, the song features four layered bass flutes blowing long, low-register tones that rattle the metal frame of the room. A drifting, tape-warped vocal enters in the final minutes, framing the genre's ultimate ethos of searching for connection across vast voids. The track fades out on a solitary question that gave the song its name: "Who left the channel markers lit when the fleet went skyward?"
